<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Musta'sim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1242">1242</a>–<a href="/years/1258">1258</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as al-Mustaʿsim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Musta'sim was the last Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> to rule from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. When Mongol forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu Khan</a> captured the city in February 1258, he was executed and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wisdom">House of Wisdom</a> was destroyed. His death ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> of Baghdad, which had ruled since 750, and cleared the way for the establishment of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-mustasim.jpg" alt="al-Musta'sim" width="320" height="143" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DrFO.Jr.Tn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinar_Abbasside_-_al-Musta%27sim_bi-llah_-_641_AH_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
